# Baseline for `bash scripts/showcase-metrics.sh --check`.
#
# `commits`, `last_commit`, and `days_span` are deliberately NOT listed here.
# Recording any of them requires a commit, and that commit changes them —
# there is no value you can write that stays correct after you write it.
# Re-baselining just produces the next-off-by-one and the check can never
# pass. The rule: a key belongs in this file only if committing this file
# does not itself change that key's measured value. `commits`/`last_commit`/
# `days_span` still appear in the script's *output* — they are published
# figures, just not part of the pass/fail gate. Do not add them back.
#
# This baseline tracks the LIVE repository. The table published in
# ENGINEERING-PRACTICE.md is pinned to commit `72c312f`, so the two are
# expected to diverge as work lands — and today they do: `specs` and `plans`
# read 25/28 here against a published 24/27, because one spec and one plan
# were added after that commit. Neither number is wrong. A drift reported
# here means the live repo moved; it is not a signal that the published
# figure needs correcting. Re-pin the published table only when it is
# deliberately re-measured against a new commit.
version: 0.24.1
rust_tests: 680
vitest_tests: 198
tests_total: 878
specs: 25
plans: 28
gotchas: 13
workflows: 3
backends: 3
